"sha":"dc46328f0a8d8ff9d4b18fa39462d59979df8abd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tanpn2402/hr-hub/commits/dc46328f0a8d8ff9d4b18fa39462d59979df8abd"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tanpn2402/hr-hub/commits/bccfe96a54ce29e46f81989adc86221d5ff21617/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T03:23:24Z","email":"tan.pham@tx-tech.com","name":"Tan Pham"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T03:23:24Z","email":"tan.pham@tx-tech.com","name":"Tan Pham"},"message":"feat: enhance API response handling for JSON fields\n\n- Implemented parsing for JSON-serialized fields in realms, registration fields, SAML service providers, service accounts, webhooks, and wizard states to ensure consistent data structures across the application.\n- Added utility functions `parseJsonArray`, `parseJsonObject`, `stringifyJsonArray`, and `stringifyJsonObject` to handle JSON parsing and stringifying for SQLite compatibility.\n- Updated API endpoints to utilize new mapping functions for transforming raw API responses into expected formats.\n- Introduced comprehensive unit tests for JSON utility functions to ensure robustness and reliability.\n- Adjusted Vite configuration for the admin UI and web applications to point to the correct backend service.\n- Enhanced error handling in the AuthFlowService to fallback to default flow steps on validation failure.\n- Updated client controller and service to parse JSON fields before returning responses to ensure clients receive correctly formatted data.","tree":{"sha":"4cbe9e629bed2102c062e7a16b78418655e93c6d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tanpn2402/hr-hub/git/trees/4cbe9e629bed2102c062e7a16b78418655e93c6d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tanpn2402/hr-hub/git/commits/bccfe96a54ce29e46f81989adc86221d5ff21617","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/tanpn2402/hr-hub/commit/bccfe96a54ce29e46