.github.com/users/geep97/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/geep97","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ADANSEORG/adanse-frontend/commits/d795bed09304650550c86c0b77d0970bf1d15acf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T09:27:42Z","email":"owusugodman@gmail.com","name":"geep97"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T09:27:42Z","email":"owusugodman@gmail.com","name":"geep97"},"message":"Retry transient failures quietly and never show raw error text\n\nResearchers were seeing raw messages like \"Could not complete that\nrequest\" and \"Failed to fetch\", usually right after signing in.\n\n- Read requests (GET) are retried quietly on a dropped connection or a\n  momentary server error (500/502/503/504), waiting 1s, 2s, 4s, 8s,\n  before any error is shown. Writes are never retried (a save, upload or\n  payment must not run twice). downloadChapter4 is untouched (it charges\n  credits).\n- friendly() never shows raw technical text: dropped connections get a\n  plain connection message; generic server failures and errors from the\n  app''s own code get a plain \"something went wrong\" (or the screen''s own\n  fallback). Specific messages (payments, file too large, sign-in) still\n  come through.\n- Account, sign-in, reset-password and qualitative-review screens now use\n  friendly() instead of showing err.message directly.\n- The sign-in load fetches projects and credits independently, so one\n  failing doesn''t discard the other.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0b22936fee8a5d6b17dde5511b213fae2da51378","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ADANSEORG/adanse-frontend/git/trees/0b22936fee8a5d6b17dde5511b213fae2da51378"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ADANSEORG/adanse-frontend/git/commits/d795bed09304650550c86c0b77d0970bf1d15acf","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer"