ents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ADANSEORG/adanse-frontend/commits/a6c18cd0f89daeef3fff49625cb2f9f28d61c8fc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T16:57:41Z","email":"owusugodman@gmail.com","name":"geep97"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T16:57:41Z","email":"owusugodman@gmail.com","name":"geep97"},"message":"Review screen: tick rating questions to reverse their scores\n\nBackend #68 lets a scored rating question be reverse-scored. On the review\nscreen, the \"Scored a rating scale\" entry now lists its questions with a\ntick box each:\n\n- The reason ends by pointing to the boxes (\"tick it below to reverse its\n  scores\") instead of \"must be reversed by you\".\n- Changing the ticks shows \"Apply these changes\"; a confirmation says what\n  will be reversed (and that 5 becomes 1, 4 becomes 2) or put back, that it\n  creates a new version to validate and activate, and -- on the active\n  version -- that analysis resets and what re-running costs.\n- Applying sends the full set that should end up reversed for that grid\n  (another grid''s reversals kept, its unapplied ticks not sent) to\n  POST .../reverse-scores and moves to the new version, where the reversed\n  questions show \"Reversed\". Unticking one puts it back the same way.\n- A reversal is not listed as a separate \"fixed\" step: the grid shows it.\n- Only a cleaned or validated version can be changed, as with the\n  personal-data actions.\n\nChecked: 267 unit tests (new reverseScores.test.js, cleaningSteps additions)\nand 13 checks in a real browser against a mock that follows #68''s rules:\ntick/Apply/confirm/Cancel, the request body and version, the Reversed\nstate after applying, restoring with an empty set.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"cf06852d3d87505efb92fdab484a1b495748008d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ADANSEORG/adanse-frontend/git/trees/cf06852d3d87505efb92fdab484a1b495748008d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/rep