":"https://github.com/ADANSEORG/adanse-frontend/commit/000caeff45f205709aaf49c56a32507a3688dc7e","node_id":"C_kwDOUYV0zNoAKDAwMGNhZWZmNDVmMjA1NzA5YWFmNDljNTZhMzI1MDdhMzY4OGRjN2U","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ADANSEORG/adanse-frontend/commit/dc95377848eb3b9ceb05fce5232ac730919a3e0f","sha":"dc95377848eb3b9ceb05fce5232ac730919a3e0f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ADANSEORG/adanse-frontend/commits/dc95377848eb3b9ceb05fce5232ac730919a3e0f"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/ADANSEORG/adanse-frontend/commit/8f2a0ce61b7fff85252642d456e68ea30ce269f5","sha":"8f2a0ce61b7fff85252642d456e68ea30ce269f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ADANSEORG/adanse-frontend/commits/8f2a0ce61b7fff85252642d456e68ea30ce269f5"}],"sha":"000caeff45f205709aaf49c56a32507a3688dc7e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ADANSEORG/adanse-frontend/commits/000caeff45f205709aaf49c56a32507a3688dc7e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71272701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geep97/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geep97/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geep97/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geep97/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/geep97","id":71272701,"login":"geep97","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxMjcyNzAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geep97/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geep97/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geep97/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geep97/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geep97/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/geep97","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ADANSEORG/adanse-frontend/commits/8fcb4091eaa0aed1e3e428f4ee8750263d9f6d8c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T12:00:52Z","email":"owusugodman@gmail.com","name":"geep97"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T12:00:52Z","email":"owusugodman@gmail.com","name":"geep97"},"message":"Project routes, PR 3/4: review and analysis\n\nThird of four PRs building Stage 2 (see PR 1 #59, PR 2 #60, and the\nreal-routes-plan memory note). Review and analysis join setup/dataset as real\nroutes -- /project/:id/review and /project/:id/analysis -- so reloading either,\nor opening one as a deep link, stays on that screen. Chapter4 is not routed yet\n(PR 4, with its gate); a bare /project/:id landing on chapter4''s outcome still\njust normalizes to the bare id, as before.\n\n- ROUTED_STEPS gains \"review\" and \"analysis\"; select()''s requestedStep\n  handling (resolveProjectStep vs. defaultProjectStep) now covers both.\n- The pending-version fetch that decides \"review\" is broadened: it already\n  ran when a dataset is uploaded but not yet active (unchanged); it now ALSO\n  runs whenever \"review\" is explicitly requested, even on a project that\n  already has an active_dataset_version_id -- a re-grouping or a\n  declared-type change after activation creates a fresh version needing its\n  own review (see backend #67), and a bookmark or reload landing on /review\n  needs to know about that, which the narrower pre-existing trigger never\n  would have.\n- file() (upload), activateDataset() and build()''s success path each push\n  their new step''s URL; goReviewPendingDataset() (build''s 409 handler, its\n  only remaining caller) now replaces to /review -- a correction, not the\n  destination the researcher asked for.\n- Two new history-aware Back handlers, same shape as PR 2''s backToSetup:\n  backFromReview (-> dataset) and backFromAnalysis (-> review if a dataset\n  version is known, else dataset, matching the pre-routing rule). The\n  Chapter4 Back branch is untouched.\n- Qualitative review/finalize needed no new code: QualitativeReview.jsx\n  already fetches its own session on mount and resumes polling on its own\n  when it mounts mid-\"finalizing\" (pre-existing, documented behaviour). What\n  changes is that a reload now actually reaches that component instead of\n  the blank form, making this reachable via reload for the first time --\n  verified in the browser harness below, not re-implemented.\n\nChecked in a real browser (mock backend, headless Edge): 13 checks, including\nan already-active project with a newer pending version still opening Review\n(the broadened check above, not just wiring); reload staying put on both new\nroutes; a full review -> validate -> activate -> analysis walk-through with\nhistory-aware Back at each step; and reload mid-qualitative-finalize landing on\nAnalysis with the finalizing state shown. The same harness fails on the\npre-PR3 code (4 of its checks), and two targeted mutations (narrowing the\npending-version fetch back to its old trigger, dropping activateDataset''s\nnavigate) are each caught by exactly the check meant to catch them.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d4fa6a2dc141152dd3e2da84f6e23b03cd86d9ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ADANSEORG/adanse-frontend/git/trees/d4fa6a2dc141152dd3e2da84f6e23b03cd86d9ea"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ADANSEORG/adanse-frontend/git/commits/8fcb4091eaa0aed1e3e428f4ee8750263d9f6d8c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71272701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geep97/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geep97/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geep97/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geep97/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/geep97","id":71272701,"login":"geep97","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxMjcyNzAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geep97/orgs","received_event