/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geep97/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geep97/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/geep97","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ADANSEORG/adanse-frontend/commits/d1114acce13017c53c9de7737beecabf5c0b4cb5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T14:24:48Z","email":"owusugodman@gmail.com","name":"geep97"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T14:24:48Z","email":"owusugodman@gmail.com","name":"geep97"},"message":"Replace the pin \\\"...\\\" menu with a direct pin/unpin icon button\n\nThe three-dots menu held exactly one action, so pinning took two clicks\nfor no reason. Each sidebar item now has a pin icon: one click pins, and a\npinned item shows a gold unpin icon that unpins on one click (no\nconfirmation -- it only clears the pin).\n\n- Shown on hover/active/keyboard focus like the delete \"x\", and always\n  visible on touch devices. Disabled while its request is in flight so a\n  double click can''t send it twice.\n- Removes the menu, popover, outside-click handling and their CSS. The\n  title marquee no longer needs its \"pause while menu open\" case.\n- A rejected pin still shows the backend''s message in the sidebar notice.\n\nChecked in a headless browser: pin moves the row to Pinned and flips the\nicon; unpin returns it to its date group.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1aacd87382fe6f4d408e5b10d72ebd145608eed7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ADANSEORG/adanse-frontend/git/trees/1aacd87382fe6f4d408e5b10d72ebd145608eed7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ADANSEORG/adanse-frontend/git/commits/d1114acce13017c53c9de7737beecabf5c0b4cb5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71272701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geep97/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geep97/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geep97/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geep97/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/geep97","id":71272701,"login":"geep97","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxMjcyNzAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geep97/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geep97/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geep97/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geep97/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geep97/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/geep97","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ADANSEORG/adanse-frontend/commit/d1114acce13017c53c9de7737beecabf5c0b4cb5","node_id":"C_kwDOUYV0zNoAKGQxMTE0YWNjZTEzMDE3YzUzYzlkZTc3MzdiZWVjYWJmNWMwYjRjYjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ADANSEORG/adanse-frontend/commit/2de8c50d0e141003b98fee3d9452f54bbb7de575","sha":"2de8c50d0e141003b98fee3d9452f54bbb7de575","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ADANSEORG/adanse-frontend/commits/2de8c50d0e141003b98fee3d9452f54bbb7de575"}],"sha":"d1114acce13017c53c9de7737beecabf5c0b4cb5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ADANSEORG/adanse-frontend/commits/d1114acce13017c53c9de7737beecabf5c0b4cb5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71272701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geep97/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geep97/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geep97/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geep97/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/geep97","id":71272701,"login":"geep97","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxMjcyNzAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geep97/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geep97/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geep97/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geep97/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geep97/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/geep97","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ADANSEORG/adanse-frontend/commits/2de8c50d0e141003b98fee3d9452f54bbb7de575/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T14:21:51Z","email":"owusugodman@gmail.com","name":"geep97"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T14:21:51Z","email":"owusugodman@gmail.com","name":"geep97"},"message":"Slide long sidebar titles into view on hover instead of truncating them\n\nTitles that fit stay static. A title wider than its container is cut off\nwith a soft right-edge fade (CSS mask, no ellipsis) at rest; on hover or\nkeyboard focus it slides left by exactly its overflow so the end is\nreadable, then slides back. Both edges fade while scrolled.\n\n- Motion is a CSS transform transition (no JS animation loop) at a\n  constant ~40px/s with a 1.5s minimum, after a 300ms delay so skimming\n  the list doesn''t set everything moving. The mask fades are registered\n  custom properties so they ease in with the same delay.\n- The math (marqueeShift) is pure and unit-tested. The distance is\n  measured when a row becomes active, using layout widths so a\n  half-finished slide can''t skew it.\n- No scrolling on touch (hover: none) or prefers-reduced-motion: they keep\n  the static fade, and the full title is available via a title tooltip on\n  overflowing titles.\n- Works with the pin \"...\" menu and delete confirm: the slide pauses while\n  that row''s menu is open, the delete confirm replaces the row (so nothing\n  moves), and hover/focus state is cleared when the confirm opens. The\n  title area still shrinks correctly for the \"...\" and x buttons.\n\n7 new tests (127 total). Checked in a headless browser: fitting titles\nstatic and untagged, exact overflow distance, constant speed, reduced-\nmotion keeps the fade with no movement, keyboard focus triggers the slide.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"794f7342e509b829a714e16a8bfee18e02017c71","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ADANSEORG/adanse-frontend/git/trees/794f7342e509b829a714e16a8bfee18e02017c71"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ADANSEORG/adanse-frontend/git/commits/2de8c50d0e141003b98fee3d9452f54bbb7de575","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71272701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geep97/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geep97/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geep97/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geep97/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/geep97","id":71272701,"login":"geep97","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxMjcyNzAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geep97/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geep97/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geep97/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geep97/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geep97/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/geep97","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ADANSEORG/adanse-frontend/commit/2de8c50d0e141003b98fee3d9452f54bbb7de575","node_id":"C_kwDOUYV0zNoAKDJkZThjNTBkMGUxNDEwMDNiOThmZWUzZDk0NTJmNTRiYmI3ZGU1NzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ADANSEORG/adanse-frontend/commit/e6e4e71676c790dfba4a54d8cc8d5d0ae67b5f88","sha":"e6e4e71676c790dfba4a54d8cc8d5d0ae67b5f88","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ADANS