rl":"https://api.github.com/users/Unconfirmed2/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Unconfirmed2/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Unconfirmed2/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Unconfirmed2/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Unconfirmed2","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Unconfirmed2/Proxima-MultiAI/commits/7b49b1c46069f7356814a25531fc5029e889536e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-03T10:36:45Z","email":"eugene.turetsky@gmail.com","name":"Eugene Turetsky"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-03T10:36:45Z","email":"eugene.turetsky@gmail.com","name":"Eugene Turetsky"},"message":"Multi-AI Chat: MCP multiai_* tools for Claude Desktop/Claude Code/Codex; real Stop via engine abort\n\n- src/mcp/tools-multiai.js: multiai_list_chats, multiai_read_chat, multiai_create_chat, multiai_post_message, multiai_run_round, multiai_wait_for_run, multiai_stop — via new multiai* IPC actions in main-v2.cjs, backed by a shared api object in ipc/multiai.cjs that the REST routes now use too (plus POST /wait).\n\n- Engines expose abort(); send() is wrapped so a user cancel rejects with ''Cancelled by user'' (terminal, not retried) and Gemini''s self-heal retry is suppressed after a cancel. sender.abortActive(provider, conversationId) aborts only the matching in-flight call; options.shouldRun skips queued ones. Stop in the tab, REST and MCP all go through it; in Delta mode the cancelled provider gets a fresh thread.\n\n- Tests: 77 across ipc/providers/mcp for the new paths; full suite 671/671.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01ACdKJmXfzvwfCCLneCWd12","tree":{"sha":"a2e117b0b1fb182d27f652e003e847a5a1dbdf8e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Unconfirmed2/Proxima-MultiAI/git/trees/a2e117b0b1fb182d27f652e003e847a5a1dbdf8e"},"url":"h