ary/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/seanmccleary","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Unconfirmed2/Proxima-MultiAI/commits/09296a2d308f0840fe965afbdba65dce77c853ee/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-10T10:48:37Z","email":"sean.mccleary@gmail.com","name":"Sean McCleary"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-01T13:26:28Z","email":"sean.mccleary@gmail.com","name":"Sean McCleary"},"message":"fix: normalize non-string message content to prevent [Object object] coercion\n\nWhen clients like openclaw send OpenAI-format messages where the content\nfield is an array of content parts (e.g., [{type: ''text'', text: ''...''}])\nrather than a plain string, the extractMessage function returned the raw\nobject. Downstream provider engines expected a string, causing JavaScript\nto coerce it to ''[object Object]''.\n\nAdded normalizeContent() helper that handles:\n- String passthrough (no change to existing behavior)\n- OpenAI content-part arrays (extracts text from type:''text'' parts)\n- Objects with .text or .content fields\n- Fallback to JSON.stringify for unknown structures\n\nApplied in both REST API (extractMessage) and WebSocket server\n(handleWSMessage) message extraction paths.","tree":{"sha":"b7b8e9d8ab7897e4cd994ce5c8df8ce8cdc8883b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Unconfirmed2/Proxima-MultiAI/git/trees/b7b8e9d8ab7897e4cd994ce5c8df8ce8cdc8883b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Unconfirmed2/Proxima-MultiAI/git/commits/09296a2d308f0840fe965afbdba65dce77c853ee","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1424583?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seanmccleary/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seanmccleary/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seanmccleary/following{/other_user}","gists_url":